<title>USA: Wyman-Gordon names Whelan president.</title>
<headline>Wyman-Gordon names Whelan president.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH GRAFTON, Mass 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wyman-Gordon Co said Wednesday that J. Douglas Whelan will become president and chief operating officer on October 15, succeeding David Gruber, who is now president and chief executive.</p>
<p>Whelan is now the president of the Wyman-Gordon forgings division.</p>
<p>Gruber will remain chief executive, but he will become chairman on that date, when Chairman John Nelson retires, the company said.</p>
<p>Wyman-Gordon makes advanced forgings, investment castings and composites structures for the commercial and defense aerospace, commercial power and energy and performance products markets.</p>
</text>
